WEBVTT

00:00:00.018 --> 00:00:02.572
Performance should come after correctness.

00:00:02.572 --> 00:00:07.902
A faster query that changes row grain or NULL behavior is not an improvement.

00:00:07.902 --> 00:00:10.677
Write the clearest correct query first.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:15.047
Then inspect the execution plan and consider rewrites or indexes.

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:19.602
Whenever you rewrite a subquery, compare the result sets carefully.

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:23.427
SQL can express the same logic in several forms.

00:00:23.427 --> 00:00:29.177
A good rewrite keeps the same grain and business meaning while changing how work is organized.

00:00:29.177 --> 00:00:34.922
Use EXPLAIN to inspect the plan rather than assuming one style is always faster.

00:00:34.922 --> 00:00:38.768
Performance reasoning should follow correctness, not replace it.
